# {{ project_name }} fuzzing

Coverage-guided [Atheris](https://github.com/google/atheris) fuzz harnesses for
the parsers in `{{ module_name }}` that consume untrusted external input.
Fuzzing feeds the OpenSSF Scorecard "Fuzzing" signal.

## The fuzzing model

Harnesses are written ONCE here and consumed by two tiers:

| Tier | Scope | Where |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **ClusterFuzzLite** | all repos, per-PR bounded run in CI | `.github/workflows/cifuzz.yml` + `.clusterfuzzlite/` |
| **Google OSS-Fuzz** | Apache/OSS repos only, hosted continuous fuzzing | `oss-fuzz/` (one-time onboarding PR to google/oss-fuzz) |

OSS-Fuzz only accepts open-source projects, so the `oss-fuzz/` directory is
generated **only for Apache-2.0 repos**. PolyForm-Noncommercial repos get
ClusterFuzzLite alone.

## Conventions

`atheris` is an optional, fuzz-only dependency (`pip install '.[fuzz]'`): it is
NOT in the `dev` extra or the release gate, and it ships amd64-Linux wheels
only. Harness files are named `fuzz_*.py`, so `pytest` never collects them, and
every harness imports `atheris` behind a guard so the module still imports where
`atheris` is absent. `.clusterfuzzlite/build.sh` compiles every
`tests/fuzz/fuzz_*.py` automatically — add one harness per untrusted-input
boundary.

## Run a harness locally

Atheris requires Linux with Clang and an amd64 host.

```bash
# Install the fuzz-only dependency group.
uv pip install -e '.[fuzz]'

# Fuzz one parser for 60 seconds.
python tests/fuzz/fuzz_target.py -max_total_time=60

# Reproduce a crash from a saved input.
python tests/fuzz/fuzz_target.py path/to/crash-input
```

## ClusterFuzzLite in CI

Pull requests that touch `src/`, the harnesses, or the fuzzing setup run a
short, bounded ClusterFuzzLite session via `.github/workflows/cifuzz.yml`. The
build image and build script live under `.clusterfuzzlite/`.
